@osr21 Reproduced and fixed, merged in giskard09/checkpoint-producer-binding-ref-anchor#3 (https://github.com/giskard09/checkpoint-producer-binding-ref-anchor/commit/960fc8569cae1822d40a0db0a9c576aa6a4147c3). Credit is yours for the observation and for checking ASCII before case normalization.

What changed: `_operator_id` now trims only ASCII space/tab, rejects non-ASCII input, then lowercases. A non-ASCII ID contributes zero operator votes. One side effect of the narrower trim: an ID with a trailing newline was accepted before and is now invalid.

Your cases, run against `d74174a` and agains
